[[File:Foulborn unique example.png|thumb|An example of a Foulborn unique. The mana on hit modifier is replaced in this example.]]
A '''Foulborn unique item''' is a mutated version of an existing [[unique item]] that has one or more of its modifiers replaced with different ones. Foulborn unique items can be obtained from [[Breach]] related content, primarily [[the Genesis Tree]] using an {{il|Ancient Wombgift}} or Grasping Coffers in Hive Fortresses.

__TOC__

==Mechanics==
[[File:3-to-1 Foulborn unique.png|thumb|A Foulborn unique from using the 3-to-1 recipe with its cosmetic identifiers missing. The Foulborn modifier is still intact.]]
Foulborn uniques have the prefix "Foulborn" in front of the unique item's name. They also gain the [[File:Foulborn-item-symbol.png]] on the item's name plate and the 2D artwork gains a purple effect, somewhat similar to [[Replica unique item]]s. However, Foulborn unique do not have their own slots in [[Unique Collection Tab]], and official trade site treats Foulborn unique as the same item as the original, with the exception of the "Is Foulborn" filter.

Foulborn uniques will have one or more of their modifiers replaced by Foulborn modifiers (also known as "mutated modifiers"), listed in purple. The Foulborn modifier that is added is directly correlated with the original modifier that was replaced. For example, if {{il|Quill Rain}}'s {{c|mod|(50-100)% increased Projectile Speed}} is replaced, it will always result in the Foulborn modifier {{c|foulborn|(40-60)% increased Area of Effect}}.

Foulborn items are otherwise functionally identical to their regular versions. If an {{il|Ancient Orb}} is used, it will result in a non-Foulborn unique item outcome. 

As of 3.27.0c, it is no longer possible to use the 3-to-1 [[vendor recipe]] to obtain a new copy with randomized roll values. Previously, doing so would remove the "Foulborn" text in the item's name, the name plate icons, and the purple 2D art texture. The Foulborn modifier itself would still be intact and functional. Foulborn uniques are ''not'' interchangeable for their regular versions with any recipes.

Only a select number of unique items have Foulborn variants. In general, [[drop-restricted]] uniques, such as most boss uniques, cannot be Foulborn<ref name="Keepers" />, with the exception of [[Breach item|Breach-specific unique items]].

Some ''but not all'' [[Breach item]]s share the same regular modifier stats and ID between their "regular" and "upgraded" versions, allowing the Foulborn modifier(s) to be found on both versions. For example, {{c|mod|Gain (6-10)% of Fire Damage as Extra Chaos Damage}} found on {{il|The Red Dream}} and {{il|The Red Nightmare}} can become either {{c|foulborn|+4% to Chaos Resistance per Endurance Charge}} (Jewel85=The Red Dream's Foulborn mod) or {{c|foulborn|Fire Damage with Hits is Lucky if you've Blocked an Attack Recently}} (Jewel86=The Red Nightmare's Foulborn mod).

Foulborn [[Afarud unique]]s can only be obtained from Breaches in a [[Mirage Area]]. Foulborn [[restored Maraketh unique|Maraketh unique]]s can only be obtained by using a {{il|Coin of Restoration}} on a Foulborn Afarud unique. These items cannot be obtained from other sources of Foulborn unique items.

==Acquisition==
Foulborn uniques can be obtained through the following methods:

* Birthing an {{il|Ancient Wombgift}} at [[the Genesis Tree]]
** Genesis passives can influence the outcomes that are generated (e.g. towards a specific item class or towards/against a specific attribute requirement) as well as having a chance for multiple Foulborn modifiers
** The unique is generated first; if it has a Foulborn variant, it then has a base ~20% chance to become Foulborn, which can be increased or reduced by the Genesis Tree.
* Sometimes when opening a Grasping Coffer [[chest]] in a [[Hive Fortress]] or [[Hive Colony]]
** Has an increased chance to be a [[Breach item|Breach-specific unique items]]
* Guaranteed Foulborn [[Breach item|Breach-specific unique]] drop from [[It That Was Esh]] and [[It That Was Esh]] in a [[Hive Colony]]
* Transportation [[Safehouse]]s with [[It That Fled]] stationed contains a trapped chest with Foulborn unique items
* Foulborn [[Mirage]] unique items can only be acquired from Breaches in [[Mirage]]s

